      "summary": "Section 3.2.1 states the replay-vs-mirror finding-authority invariant only for the 'Codex-Korrekturauftrag', and Slice 1 Arbeitsschritt 4 repeats 'vor dem Aufbau eines nativen Codex-Korrekturauftrags'. In the current code (workflow.py _run_codex, lines ~1493-1535), CODEX_PLAN_REVISION is dispatched under NativeCodexRequestKind.PLAN, not NativeCodexRequestKind.CORRECTION, which is reserved for CODEX_CORRECTION/CODEX_FINAL_CORRECTION. A literal reading of 3.2.1/Arbeitsschritt 4 could therefore be implemented as applying the mirror-vs-replay integrity check only to CORRECTION-kind requests, silently exempting plan-revision requests even though 3.3.5 asserts all three variants share one finding lifecycle. Confirmed against the repository: history.findings, which feeds _native_codex_request, is currently populated by orchestrator.py:_history() from state.runtime_history (the state-v3 mirror), not from a record-chain replay -- so today there is no replay-derived authority check on any Codex request path, and the plan must bind the new check to all Codex-bearing request kinds explicitly, including the PLAN kind used for revisions.",
