    "dimensions": "Verified against repository state at base commit 0448788: (1) contract closure -- schemas/native-agent-codex-result-v1.schema.json plan_result currently has no finding_dispositions field (additionalProperties:false), confirming the plan's stated Vertrags-Gap is real; (2) backward compatibility -- plan's 'historical plan_result without the field reads as empty sequence' approach is schema-additive and testable; (3) reviewer-owned finding authority -- src/artifact_models.py FindingTransitionPayload.__post_init__ already enforces 'only the reporting reviewer may mutate a finding' and 'only codex may record a finding response' with finding_status forced to stay open on a codex response, matching 3.2.4/3.2.6 without new record types; (4) record/state precedence -- orchestrator.py:_history() currently derives WorkflowHistory.findings from state.runtime_history (state-v3 mirror), not from record-chain replay, confirming the plan's own repository-Befund and validating that Slice 1 Arbeitsschritt 4 is necessary new work, not already-solved; a precedent pattern for pure record-chain finding derivation already exists in final_review_preflight.py (latest_findings built by scanning FindingTransitionPayload records) that Slice 1 can reuse; (5) request/fingerprint binding -- native_codex_request.py already threads open_findings from previous_findings into every native Codex request regardless of kind, so the transport plumbing pre-exists and only the plan_result response side and the mirror-vs-replay authority check are missing; (6) exact-once/crash recovery -- orchestrator.py already exposes recover_pending_native_codex and recover_pending_native_reviewer with record-ahead raw-response persistence for both roles individually, supporting the plan's claim that Slice 2 only needs to chain and fault-inject existing mechanisms rather than invent new ones; (7) legacy isolation -- docs/internal/native-agent-json-manueller-bootstrap.md explicitly states it does not use